This package is a Go port of the ITU-R P.372 radio noise library (P372.dll
and the ReadFamDud() coefficient reader), part of the ITU-R HF propagation
software (ITURHFProp / P533 / P372) developed collaboratively by
participants in ITU-R Study Group 3, Working Party 3L (ITU-R WP3L).

The original software states that it "may be used by implementers in their
implementation of the Recommendation as well as in revisions of the specific
original Recommendation and in other ITU Recommendations, free from any copyright
assertions", and is provided "as is" WITH NO WARRANTIES, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED.
The ITU shall not be held liable in any event for any damages arising out of
or related to use of the software.

Modifications:
  - Translated from C to Go, one Go file per original C source file.
  - Dynamically allocated arrays replaced by fixed-size Go arrays held in a
    read-only Coefficients value, so that Compute is safe for concurrent use.
  - Return codes mapped to Go error values.
  - Only the arrays used for noise (fakp, fakabp, dud, fam) are read from
    the COEFFxxW.txt monthly files; the other ionospheric coefficient arrays
    read by the stand-alone ReadCoeff() utility are not used and not ported.
  - The data files are not part of this repository; their directory is given
    at run time.
